# EXERCISE 3
# Write a program that calculates and prints the total number of
# seconds you have lived.
# Use three variables: years, months, and days.
# Convert each of the variables to seconds, and then add them
# up to obtain the final result.
# Again, remember to use str() when printing numbers.
#
# How to convert each component to component to seconds:
# - years to seconds = years * 365 * 24 * 60 * 60
# - months to seconds = months * 30 * 24 * 60 * 60
# - days to seconds = days * 24 * 60 * 60

